---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolSchema from '../../components/ToolSchema.astro';
const example = `{
    "runtimes": {
        "nvidia": {
            "path": "nvidia-container-runtime",
            "runtimeArgs": []
        }
    },
    "shutdown-timeout": 60
}`;
---
<Base image="/og/tool-docker-log-limits.png" title="Docker log size limit helper" description="Cap Docker's container logs: paste your daemon.json, choose max-size and max-file, and get the merged config plus the worst-case disk usage.">
  <ToolSchema />
  <div class="prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <h1>Docker log size limit helper</h1>
    <p class="lede">Docker keeps container logs forever by default. Paste your current <code>/etc/docker/daemon.json</code>, pick a limit, and get the merged file back, with everything you already had kept intact.</p>
    <p class="meta">Runs entirely in your browser. Nothing you paste is sent anywhere.</p>
  </div>

  <form class="tool" id="dl">
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Your current daemon.json (leave empty if you don't have one)</legend>
      <textarea name="existing" spellcheck="false" aria-label="current daemon.json">{example}</textarea>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Limits</legend>
      <label class="row"><span>Max size per log file</span>
        <select name="size"><option>10m</option><option selected>20m</option><option>50m</option><option>100m</option></select>
      </label>
      <label class="row"><span>Files kept per container</span>
        <select name="files"><option>2</option><option selected>3</option><option>5</option></select>
      </label>
      <label class="row"><span>Number of containers (for the estimate)</span>
        <select name="containers"><option>10</option><option>20</option><option selected>30</option><option>50</option><option>100</option></select>
      </label>
      <button type="submit" class="action">Generate</button>
    </fieldset>
  </form>

  <p id="estimate"></p>
  <h2>New daemon.json</h2>
  <pre class="out"><code id="out"></code></pre>
  <button type="button" class="copy" id="copy">Copy</button>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Applying it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Save it as <code>/etc/docker/daemon.json</code> (needs <code>sudo</code>). Keep a backup of the old file.</li>
      <li><code>sudo systemctl restart docker</code>: all containers restart once.</li>
      <li><strong>Recreate</strong> your containers, because log settings only apply to containers created afterwards: <code>docker compose up -d --force-recreate</code> in each stack's folder.</li>
      <li>Check: <code>docker inspect &lt;container&gt; --format '&#123;&#123;.HostConfig.LogConfig&#125;&#125;'</code></li>
    </ol>
    <p>Background and the one-liner to recreate every running stack: <a href="/blog/docker-log-size-limits/">Docker logs ate 2.4 GB on my server</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="meta tool-feedback">Found a bug or a wrong result? <a href="/contact/">Tell me</a>, or <a href="https://github.com/realFinDev/realfin-site/issues" rel="nofollow">open an issue on GitHub</a>.</p>

  <script is:inline src="/tools/docker-logs.js"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var form = document.getElementById('dl'), el = form.elements, D = window.DockerLogs;
      function update() {
        var size = el.namedItem('size').value, files = +el.namedItem('files').value, n = +el.namedItem('containers').value;
        var r = D.merge(el.namedItem('existing').value, size, files);
        var out = document.getElementById('out');
        if (!r.ok) { out.textContent = r.error; out.className = 'warn'; }
        else { out.textContent = r.json; out.className = ''; }
        var w = D.worstCase(n, size, files);
        document.getElementById('estimate').textContent = w
          ? 'Worst case: ' + D.human(w.perContainer) + ' per container, ' + D.human(w.total) + ' for ' + n + ' containers. Most containers log far less.'
          : '';
      }
      form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) { e.preventDefault(); update(); });
      form.addEventListener('change', update);
      document.getElementById('copy').addEventListener('click', function () {
        var b = this; navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('out').textContent).then(function () { b.textContent = 'Copied'; setTimeout(function () { b.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1200); });
      });
      update();
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
